<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madina Mayurqa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">903–<a href="/years/1229">1229</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Medina Mayurqa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madina Mayurqa was the Arabic name of the city now called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palma</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> under Muslim rule from 903 to 1229. It served as the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Majorca after 1076 and was sacked by a Pisan and Catalan fleet in 1115. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> captured it in 1229, after which it became the Christian city of Palma.</p></div>
